# What `vercel deploy` must not upload.
#
# `.gitignore` does NOT reliably cover this — the Vercel CLI uploads the working directory
# and wants its own list, so a 225MB `workie.db` sitting untracked beside the source is still
# offered to the platform and trips the 100MB limit with `File size limit exceeded`.
#
# None of this belongs in a deployment anyway. The hosted app reads Turso, never a local
# SQLite file; the corpus lives on the GitHub Actions runner and is mirrored up from there.

# The corpus and its WAL sidecars — hundreds of megabytes, and the wrong data source for
# the deployed app besides.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Cycle logs, rotated daily by scripts/refresh.sh. Local-only diagnostics.
/logs

# Recorded connector responses, replayed by the offline test suite. Not runtime data.
/fixtures/live

# Build output and dependencies: Vercel produces its own.
/.next
/node_modules
